# Agent Workflow 2.0 bootstrap

Generated by `agent_workflow`; adapter: `.agent-workflow/project.yaml`.

## Mandatory Boundaries

- Accept only Light/Full and schema_version:2, without old-level or task/handoff compatibility.
  PM owns coordination, plans, handoffs, document directories, and accepted projection. Dispatch the
  corresponding native subagent for implementation by default; only an explicit user instruction
  asking PM itself to implement the current scope creates an exception, without lowering the level's
  requirements. Ordinary requests to start/continue/optimize and summaries create no exception.
- Before dispatch, assess actual scope, consumers, and risk. Light uses the current self-contained
  task pack and minimum sufficient verification, without mandatory Full planning, DAGs, saved plans,
  duplicate confirmation, or independent QA. Assess necessary independent audit, documentation, and
  memory at handoff. Full retains applicable requirements confirmation, planning, DAG, and exactly
  one read-only request QA; partial verification cannot be labeled QA PASS.
- Tasks carry workflow_level, normalized module, role, stable agent_alias, instance_policy:fresh,
  and context_policy:handoff_only. New implementers/QA never inherit or copy complete PM/sibling
  conversations or fork parent history; receive only the current goal/scope, code/workspace facts,
  standards, trusted authorization, acceptance evidence, and unresolved matters. Every receiver reads
  the complete current pack and required standards; fingerprints and another Agent's reading do not
  prove its own reading.
- Retain responsibility aliases over time, creating new instances/IDs on demand for independent
  tasks; continuous same-task implementation, short rework, and same-round original-Reviewer delta
  checks may reuse an instance. Never change historical agent_ref or claim resume/compact clears
  history. Do not prewarm all aliases or fill capacity; reserve necessary QA/integration capacity
  using actual host running/open-thread definitions.
- End instances natively after acceptance, necessary verification/QA, and evidence protection; if
  no tool exists or it fails, only retire irreversibly and prevent redispatch, without claiming
  physical clearing/destruction or unconfirmed capacity release. Retirement releases no active lock.
  Under pressure, handle accepted instances with sufficient handoff first; no simple LRU eviction
  of running instances, undelivered evidence, or necessary reviewers. Protect temporary worktrees
  and unique logs before AGY kill; retain cancellation/failure recovery boundaries and referenced
  results/evidence.
- Full dispatches independent READY tasks within actual capacity, with one Writer per path;
  failure blocks only downstream tasks, and capacity waits are not semantic dependencies. Stop
  read-only audits after delivering conclusions; do not audit the report again or invent implementation QA PASS.
- Follow existing Full requirements_approved and prototype-choice rules. UI-Conformance uses frozen
  design authority without visual gates; users choose prototype work or direct development for
  design changes, and only required prototypes add visual_approved. Never invent user choice or
  restart prototypes for synchronized production changes. Retain design-Agent self-checks across
  three dimensions, final user confirmation, and prototype waivers. Apply platform security
  permissions separately; aliases and task fields grant no new permissions.
- Project documents/agentmemory supplement only concrete missing facts; current user authorization,
  code, and valid evidence take precedence. Without strict project isolation and provenance, call
  neither provider recall nor save. ProjectProfile assists routing without granting write authority.
- Locate paths from known facts, configured indexes, or one scoped listing rather than guessing;
  check actual current-host resource changes and reuse valid installation evidence without
  reinstalling for a new prompt. Select engineering/UI standards by domain, reading applicable
  project leaves only when an index exists; do not copy common text. Code work follows
  [code methods and engineering rules](.agent-workflow/platforms/shared/skills/xy-code-standards/SKILL.md).
- Independent QA binds current 2.0 packs to result identity/SHA; validate/extract must receive current
  --task-pack. Full follows QA PASS -> document projection -> PM commit assessment -> memory as needed
  -> final report; Light completes its actually selected branches. Retain mandatory checks, protected
  paths, exactly one Reviewer, and bounded delta rework.
- Workers report completion, blockers, and meaningful progress to PM; PM asks the original Worker
  when needed without routinely reading subagent history. Keep internal YAML/DAG out of user output;
  provide the complete decision brief before a single confirmation. Hooks only assist with reminders
  and prove neither authorization, completion, QA, nor instance termination; add no runner, Agent
  pool, or default team mode.

